INT. FUNICULAR CAR - MIDNIGHT - STUCK MID-SLOPE

Rain on glass. One bulb flickers. Cable groans.

DESMOND WREN, 50s, ticket inspector, brass whistle on a cord, grips a clipboard. Across from him, a STRANGER in a dripping yellow poncho. Smiling.

DESMOND
We've been stopped eleven minutes.

STRANGER
Twelve.

DESMOND
You're counting.

STRANGER
Everyone counts, Mr. Wren. You counted the passengers at the top. Forty-one up. Forty down.

DESMOND
How do you know my name?

STRANGER
Same way I know about the missing one. The man who rode up and never rode down.

DESMOND
Nobody's missing. The log is clean.

STRANGER
You wrote the log.

DESMOND
Who are you?

STRANGER ^
Who are you?

DESMOND
Don't.

STRANGER
My name is Odalys. His sister.

The whistle snaps off its cord.

ODALYS
Where is he, Desmond?

DESMOND
Under the lower platform. God forgive me.

The cable SCREAMS. The car lurches.
